1
00:00:03,211 --> 00:00:05,297
HEY, HEY, HEY, HEY.

2
00:00:05,297 --> 00:00:08,258
NONE OF THAT, NOT WHILE
YOU'RE LIVING UNDER MY ROOF.

3
00:00:08,258 --> 00:00:10,218
WHAT?

4
00:00:10,218 --> 00:00:12,554
LOOK, JUST BECAUSE
I KNOW ABOUT YOU TWO

5
00:00:12,554 --> 00:00:14,682
DOESN'T MEAN I LIKE
LOOKING AT IT.

6
00:00:14,682 --> 00:00:17,351
AREN'T YOU SUPPOSED TO BE
AT AN AUDITION FOR ANOTHER HOUR?

7
00:00:17,351 --> 00:00:20,395
WELL, I'M SORRY IF I'M NOT
A MIDDLE-AGED, BLACK WOMAN.

8
00:00:22,481 --> 00:00:23,899
AND I'M ALSO SORRY

9
00:00:23,899 --> 00:00:27,987
IF SOMETIMES I GO TO
THE WRONG AUDITION.

10
00:00:27,987 --> 00:00:29,989
OKAY, LOOK, IF
I HAVE TO PRETEND
I DON'T KNOW ABOUT YOU TWO

11
00:00:29,989 --> 00:00:31,991
THEN YOU TWO ARE GOING
TO HAVE TO PRETEND

12
00:00:31,991 --> 00:00:33,492
THERE'S NOTHING TO KNOW ABOUT.

13
00:00:33,492 --> 00:00:35,661
OKAY. SORRY.
OKAY.

14
00:00:35,661 --> 00:00:36,954
SORRY.

15
00:00:40,415 --> 00:00:42,584
( soft moaning )

16
00:00:42,584 --> 00:00:44,211
I CAN
HEAR THAT!

17
00:00:45,504 --> 00:00:47,088
RACHEL'S AT WORK.

18
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:55,723
I CAN STILL
HEAR YOU!

19
00:01:02,229 --> 00:01:07,484
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

20
00:01:07,484 --> 00:01:09,820
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

21
00:01:09,820 --> 00:01:12,781
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

22
00:01:12,781 --> 00:01:17,160
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

23
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:19,120
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

24
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:22,165
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

25
00:01:22,165 --> 00:01:25,836
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

26
00:01:25,836 --> 00:01:27,922
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

27
00:01:27,922 --> 00:01:30,507
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

28
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:32,760
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

29
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:35,971
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

30
00:01:35,971 --> 00:01:41,810
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

31
00:01:44,145 --> 00:01:45,188
HEY.

32
00:01:45,188 --> 00:01:46,147
HELLO.
HEY.

33
00:01:46,147 --> 00:01:47,649
HEY. WHAT'S THAT?

34
00:01:47,649 --> 00:01:49,109
MY MOM SENT ME
A FAMILY HEIRLOOM

35
00:01:49,109 --> 00:01:50,861
THAT ONCE BELONGED
TO MY GRANDMOTHER.

36
00:01:50,861 --> 00:01:52,195
CAN YOU BELIEVE IT?

37
00:01:52,195 --> 00:01:53,822
A YEAR AGO,
I DIDN'T EVEN HAVE A FAMILY

38
00:01:53,822 --> 00:01:56,533
AND NOW I HAVE HEIRLOOMS,
FOR CRYING OUT LOUD.

39
00:02:01,789 --> 00:02:03,624
( grunting )

40
00:02:03,624 --> 00:02:04,792
HEE-HEE.

41
00:02:06,585 --> 00:02:07,711
OH! GOD!

42
00:02:07,711 --> 00:02:09,755
AH!

43
00:02:09,755 --> 00:02:12,091
OOH, SOFT.

44
00:02:13,258 --> 00:02:14,843
IS THIS MINK?
YEAH.

45
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:17,805
WHY WOULD MY MOTHER
SEND ME A FUR?

46
00:02:17,805 --> 00:02:20,641
DOESN'T SHE KNOW ME,
BUT AT ALL?!

47
00:02:20,641 --> 00:02:22,726
PLUS, I HAVE A PERFECTLY
FINE COAT

48
00:02:22,726 --> 00:02:25,186
THAT NO INNOCENT ANIMAL
SUFFERED TO MAKE.

49
00:02:25,186 --> 00:02:27,355
YEAH, JUST SOME
9-YEAR-OLD FILIPINO KIDS

50
00:02:27,355 --> 00:02:30,067
WHO WORKED THEIR FINGERS BLOODY
FOR 12 CENTS AN HOUR.

51
00:02:31,735 --> 00:02:33,403
THAT DIDN'T HAPPEN.

52
00:02:33,403 --> 00:02:34,571
I MADE THAT UP.

53
00:02:37,032 --> 00:02:38,450
HEY.

54
00:02:38,450 --> 00:02:39,451
ROSS.

55
00:02:39,451 --> 00:02:40,702
ROSS...

56
00:02:40,702 --> 00:02:42,287
YOU CAN'T PUT
UP FLIERS IN HERE.

57
00:02:42,287 --> 00:02:44,498
HOW COME?
EVERYBODY ELSE DOES.

58
00:02:44,498 --> 00:02:46,166
YOU CAN'T.

59
00:02:48,919 --> 00:02:51,212
WHAT IS THAT?

60
00:02:51,212 --> 00:02:52,798
OH, UH...

61
00:02:52,798 --> 00:02:55,134
I'M JUST GETTING RID
OF A COUPLE OF THINGS.

62
00:02:55,134 --> 00:02:57,218
THIS IS ALL OF YOUR THINGS.

63
00:02:58,637 --> 00:03:00,430
YES. YES, IT IS.

64
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:01,807
NO, BUT IT'S GOOD.

65
00:03:01,807 --> 00:03:04,434
SEE, EMILY THINKS WE SHOULD GET
ALL NEW STUFF.

66
00:03:04,434 --> 00:03:06,145
STUFF THAT'S JUST OURS,
TOGETHER.

67
00:03:06,145 --> 00:03:07,646
YOU KNOW, BRAND-NEW.

68
00:03:07,646 --> 00:03:09,148
BASICALLY, THIS IS

69
00:03:09,148 --> 00:03:10,858
A GETTING-RID-OF-ANYTHING-
RACHEL-EVER-TOUCHED SALE.

70
00:03:10,858 --> 00:03:13,861
TOUCHED, USED,
SAT ON, SLEPT ON...

71
00:03:13,861 --> 00:03:15,988
I'LL TAKE IT ALL.

72
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:19,074
HEY, ROSS,
YOU'RE OKAY WITH THAT?

73
00:03:19,074 --> 00:03:21,200
LOOK, IF I CAN JUST DO
WHAT EMILY WANTS

74
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:24,163
AND GET HER TO NEW YORK,
I'M SURE EVERYTHING
WILL BE FINE.

75
00:03:24,163 --> 00:03:26,414
BUT DON'T YOU THINK
THAT'S A LITTLE EXTREME?

76
00:03:26,414 --> 00:03:29,626
AFTER WHAT I DID,
CAN YOU BLAME HER?

77
00:03:29,626 --> 00:03:31,712
YOU GOT OFF EASY.
WHEN MY FRIEND, SILVIE'S HUSBAND

78
00:03:31,712 --> 00:03:33,630
SAID SOMEONE ELSE'S NAME IN BED

79
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:36,299
SHE CURSED HIM
AND TURNED HIS THINGIE GREEN.

80
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:45,225
WHAT IS HE DOING?

81
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:50,105
EMILY THINKS ROSS'S FURNITURE'S
GOT "RACHEL COOTIES"?

82
00:03:50,105 --> 00:03:51,815
ALL RIGHT,
CALM DOWN, JOEY.

83
00:03:51,815 --> 00:03:54,026
NO. EVERYTHING'S GETTING ALL
MESSED UP, YOU KNOW?

84
00:03:54,026 --> 00:03:56,236
EMILY WON'T LET ROSS SEE RACHEL.

85
00:03:56,236 --> 00:03:58,238
WE'RE NOT GOING TO STOP
SEEING RACHEL.

86
00:03:58,238 --> 00:04:01,116
HENCE, ROSS STOPS SEEING US.

87
00:04:01,116 --> 00:04:02,283
OH, I HATE THIS.

88
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:03,660
EVERYTHING'S CHANGING.

89
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:05,453
YEAH, I KNOW,
WE'RE LOSING ROSS.

90
00:04:05,453 --> 00:04:06,454
JOEY SAID "HENCE."

91
00:04:10,042 --> 00:04:12,044
LOOK, I'M NOT HAPPY
ABOUT THIS, EITHER

92
00:04:12,044 --> 00:04:14,295
BUT, YOU KNOW, IF
ROSS SAYS HE'S HAPPY

93
00:04:14,295 --> 00:04:16,590
THEN WE'LL JUST HAVE
TO KEEP OUR FEELINGS

94
00:04:16,590 --> 00:04:18,675
ABOUT EMILY
TO OURSELVES.

95
00:04:18,675 --> 00:04:19,968
ARE YOU COOL
WITH THAT?

96
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:21,136
NO.

97
00:04:23,013 --> 00:04:25,515
BUT, YOU KNOW, I'M AN ACTOR.

98
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:27,142
I'LL ACT COOL.

99
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:34,691
OOH...

100
00:04:34,691 --> 00:04:38,153
OH, GOD! STORAGE ROOMS
GIVE ME THE CREEPS.

101
00:04:38,153 --> 00:04:41,115
MONICA, COME ON,
PLEASE, HURRY UP.
HONEY, PLEASE.

102
00:04:41,115 --> 00:04:42,783
IF YOU WANT
THE LITTLE, ROUND WAFFLES
YOU'VE GOT TO WAIT

103
00:04:42,783 --> 00:04:44,451
TILL I FIND THE LITTLE
ROUND WAFFLE IRON.

104
00:04:45,577 --> 00:04:46,995
I WANT THE LITTLE,
ROUND WAFFLES.

105
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:48,496
ALL RIGHT.

106
00:04:48,496 --> 00:04:49,623
OH, HERE IT IS.

107
00:04:49,623 --> 00:04:53,168
RIGHT UNDERNEATH
A CAN OF BUG BOMB.

108
00:04:53,168 --> 00:04:55,212
I WONDER IF THE BEST PLACE TO
PUT SOMETHING THAT COOKS FOOD

109
00:04:55,212 --> 00:04:57,172
IS UNDERNEATH 
THE CAN OF POISON?

110
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:01,135
YOU KNOW WHAT?
I'LL HAVE TOAST.

111
00:05:01,135 --> 00:05:03,553
( both screaming )

112
00:05:03,553 --> 00:05:04,805
OH, MY GOD!

113
00:05:04,805 --> 00:05:05,889
AH!

114
00:05:05,889 --> 00:05:07,224
FOG HIM! FOG HIM!

115
00:05:07,224 --> 00:05:08,225
( screaming )

116
00:05:08,225 --> 00:05:09,601
FOG HIM!

117
00:05:09,601 --> 00:05:11,686
( coughing )

118
00:05:14,148 --> 00:05:16,942
I DON'T KNOW WHAT
I'M GOING TO DO
ABOUT THIS COAT.

119
00:05:16,942 --> 00:05:18,944
I'LL TAKE IT.

120
00:05:18,944 --> 00:05:19,945
THAT MIGHT WORK.

121
00:05:19,945 --> 00:05:21,696
OOH, YEAH.

122
00:05:25,909 --> 00:05:28,578
HUH? ALL RIGHT,
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

123
00:05:28,578 --> 00:05:30,164
YOU'RE ON IN FIVE,
MS. MINNELLI.

124
00:05:33,250 --> 00:05:36,295
NO, NO, NO. IT'S
JUST A BIT SUDDEN.

125
00:05:36,295 --> 00:05:37,754
NO, IT'S GREAT, OKAY?

126
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:39,380
I AM TOTALLY ON BOARD.

127
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:40,590
I LOVE YOU, TOO.

128
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:41,675
ALL RIGHT, BYE.

129
00:05:45,053 --> 00:05:46,471
WHAT'S THE MATTER, ROSS?

130
00:05:46,471 --> 00:05:50,475
NOTHING. NO, NO, UH, ACTUALLY...
GREAT NEWS.

131
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:52,519
I JUST GOT OFF THE PHONE
WITH EMILY

132
00:05:52,519 --> 00:05:56,355
AND LOOKS LIKE I'M
MOVING TO A NEW APARTMENT.

133
00:05:56,355 --> 00:05:57,524
WHOO-HOO!

134
00:05:59,026 --> 00:06:00,235
WHY?

135
00:06:00,235 --> 00:06:02,696
WELL, HER THOUGHT IS,
AND I AGREE

136
00:06:02,696 --> 00:06:07,492
FRESH, NEW FURNITURE,
WHY NOT A FRESH, NEW APARTMENT?

137
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:09,494
HER COUSIN HAS
THIS GREAT PLACE TO SUBLET.

138
00:06:09,494 --> 00:06:11,121
IT'S GOT A VIEW OF THE RIVER
ON ONE SIDE

139
00:06:11,121 --> 00:06:12,664
AND COLUMBIA ON THE OTHER.

140
00:06:12,664 --> 00:06:13,915
THAT'S WAY UPTOWN.

141
00:06:13,915 --> 00:06:15,542
THAT'S LIKE
THREE TRAINS AWAY...

142
00:06:15,542 --> 00:06:17,169
WHICH IS GREAT.

143
00:06:17,169 --> 00:06:19,296
I LOVE TO RIDE THAT RAIL.

144
00:06:20,672 --> 00:06:22,757
SO YOU'RE REALLY OKAY WITH THIS?

145
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:25,593
YES. YES. I MEAN, IT'S
KIND OF FAR FROM WORK

146
00:06:25,593 --> 00:06:29,097
BUT, UH, YOU KNOW,
I'LL GET SO MUCH DONE
ON THE COMMUTE.

147
00:06:29,097 --> 00:06:32,976
I'VE BEEN GIVEN
THE GIFT OF TIME.

148
00:06:32,976 --> 00:06:36,646
YOU KNOW, THAT'S SO FUNNY
'CAUSE LAST CHRISTMAS,
I GOT THE GIFT OF SPACE.

149
00:06:38,148 --> 00:06:41,151
WE SHOULD GET THEM TOGETHER
AND MAKE A CONTINUUM.

150
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:46,740
NOW HE'S MOVING?

151
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:49,076
MAN, WHAT IS EMILY
DOING TO HIM?

152
00:06:49,076 --> 00:06:50,577
OW!

153
00:06:50,577 --> 00:06:52,996
HE'S NOT EVEN HERE!

154
00:06:54,331 --> 00:06:55,832
YOU GUYS!
YOU GUYS!

155
00:06:55,832 --> 00:06:57,918
WE WERE JUST IN
THE STORAGE AREA

156
00:06:57,918 --> 00:07:00,045
AND WE SAW THIS
REALLY CREEPY MAN.

157
00:07:00,045 --> 00:07:03,090
IT WAS LIKE THIS
CRAZY-EYED, HAIRY BEAST-MAN.

158
00:07:03,090 --> 00:07:05,175
HE WAS LIKE A...
LIKE A BIGFOOT

159
00:07:05,175 --> 00:07:06,801
OR A YETI OR SOMETHING.

160
00:07:06,801 --> 00:07:08,011
AND HE CAME AT US

161
00:07:08,011 --> 00:07:09,346
WITH AN AX,
SO RACHEL

162
00:07:09,346 --> 00:07:11,181
HAD TO USE A
BUG BOMB ON HIM.

163
00:07:11,181 --> 00:07:12,599
YEAH, I PULLED THE TAB

164
00:07:12,599 --> 00:07:14,393
AND I JUST FOGGED
HIS YETI ASS.

165
00:07:16,353 --> 00:07:18,897
UH, LIKE DARK HAIR, BUSHY BEARD?

166
00:07:18,897 --> 00:07:21,482
YEAH.
YEAH, YOU FOGGED DANNY.

167
00:07:22,984 --> 00:07:25,779
OH, PLEASE.
WE DID NOT FOG DANNY.

168
00:07:25,779 --> 00:07:27,781
WHO'S DANNY?

169
00:07:27,781 --> 00:07:29,699
DANNY JUST MOVED IN DOWNSTAIRS.

170
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:31,034
YEAH, HE JUST GOT BACK

171
00:07:31,034 --> 00:07:33,328
FROM THIS FOUR-MONTH TREK
IN THE ANDES.

172
00:07:33,328 --> 00:07:34,746
NICE FELLA.

173
00:07:34,746 --> 00:07:36,581
OH, HE'S NICE.
HE'S NICE.

174
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:38,250
YOU KNOW,
YOU ALWAYS...

175
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:40,460
STICK UP FOR THE
PEOPLE WE FOG.

176
00:07:51,096 --> 00:07:52,306
YEAH.
HI.

177
00:07:52,306 --> 00:07:53,765
YOU MIGHT NOT
REMEMBER US

178
00:07:53,765 --> 00:07:55,934
BUT WE ARE THE GIRLS
THAT FOGGED YOU.

179
00:07:55,934 --> 00:07:57,144
YEAH. WE'RE... WE'RE

180
00:07:57,144 --> 00:07:58,728
REALLY SORRY
WE FOGGED YOU.

181
00:07:58,728 --> 00:07:59,729
YEAH.

182
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:01,315
OKAY.

183
00:08:04,067 --> 00:08:05,026
HMM.

184
00:08:07,654 --> 00:08:09,697
HI. UH, JUST SO YOU KNOW

185
00:08:09,697 --> 00:08:11,574
WE... WE DIDN'T MEAN
TO FOG YOU.

186
00:08:11,574 --> 00:08:14,661
WE ACTUALLY THOUGHT YOU
WERE, LIKE, A YETI OR SOMETHING.

187
00:08:14,661 --> 00:08:16,788
OKAY.

188
00:08:20,625 --> 00:08:22,377
YES?

189
00:08:22,377 --> 00:08:24,587
HI. UH, SORRY
TO BOTHER YOU

190
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:26,423
BUT I DON'T THINK
THAT WE CAN ACCEPT

191
00:08:26,423 --> 00:08:28,342
YOUR ACCEPTANCE
OF OUR APOLOGY.

192
00:08:28,342 --> 00:08:31,052
IT JUST DOESN'T REALLY SEEM
LIKE YOU MEAN IT.
YEAH.

193
00:08:31,052 --> 00:08:33,180
OKAY.

194
00:08:36,515 --> 00:08:39,269
WOW. THAT GUY
IS SO RUDE.

195
00:08:39,269 --> 00:08:41,980
REALLY. WHAT
IS WITH THAT GUY?

196
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:44,316
I MEAN, YOU'D FORGIVE ME
IF I FOGGED YOU.

197
00:08:44,316 --> 00:08:46,443
WELL, YOU DID
A LITTLE BIT.

198
00:08:46,443 --> 00:08:48,236
OH, MY GOD.

199
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:50,071
HONEY, I'M SO SORRY.

200
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:51,490
I TOTALLY FORGIVE YOU.

201
00:08:51,490 --> 00:08:52,615
REALLY?
YEAH.

202
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:54,242
OH...

203
00:08:58,038 --> 00:08:59,331
HEY.
HEY.

204
00:08:59,331 --> 00:09:01,166
SO, LISTEN, YOU KNOW
MY FRIEND CHRIS

205
00:09:01,166 --> 00:09:02,792
WHO OWNS THE
CREMATORIUM?

206
00:09:02,792 --> 00:09:05,628
CREMATORIUM CHRIS? SURE.

207
00:09:05,628 --> 00:09:07,130
WELL, HE SAID THAT HE

208
00:09:07,130 --> 00:09:09,632
WOULD CREMATE MY
FUR COAT FOR FREE

209
00:09:09,632 --> 00:09:11,468
IF I, UM, YOU
KNOW, BRING IN

210
00:09:11,468 --> 00:09:13,553
THE NEXT PERSON
I KNOW WHO DIES.

211
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:15,889
REALLY?

212
00:09:15,889 --> 00:09:17,057
( gasping )

213
00:09:17,057 --> 00:09:18,725
OH, MY GOD.

214
00:09:18,725 --> 00:09:21,269
OH, MY GOD, LOOK
AT THESE PELTS.

215
00:09:21,269 --> 00:09:24,689
DON'T GET TOO ATTACHED.
SHE'S HAVING IT CREMATED.

216
00:09:24,689 --> 00:09:26,525
WHAT?

217
00:09:26,525 --> 00:09:29,027
PH-PHOEBE? HONEY?

218
00:09:29,027 --> 00:09:31,154
HONEY, I KNOW YOU'RE QUIRKY
AND I GET A BIG KICK OUT OF IT.

219
00:09:31,154 --> 00:09:33,156
WE ALL DO, ACTUALLY.

220
00:09:33,156 --> 00:09:35,325
BUT IF YOU DESTROY
A COAT LIKE THIS--

221
00:09:35,325 --> 00:09:38,328
I MEAN, THAT IS LIKE
A CRIME AGAINST NATURE.

222
00:09:38,328 --> 00:09:41,415
NO, NOT NATURE. FASHION.

223
00:09:41,415 --> 00:09:43,500
THIS IS FASHION?

224
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:45,919
OKAY, SO TO YOU,
DEATH IS FASHION.

225
00:09:45,919 --> 00:09:47,170
THAT'S REALLY FUNNY.

226
00:09:47,170 --> 00:09:49,256
YEAH. HERE'S... HERE'S PHOEBE

227
00:09:49,256 --> 00:09:53,176
UH, SPORTING, YOU KNOW,
A CUTTING-EDGE, HAIRY CARCASS

228
00:09:53,176 --> 00:09:57,847
FROM, YOU KNOW, THE STEEL TRAPS
OF WINTRY RUSSIA.

229
00:09:57,847 --> 00:10:01,184
I MEAN, YOU REALLY THINK
THIS LOOKS GOOD?

230
00:10:01,184 --> 00:10:03,270
'CAUSE I DO.

231
00:10:07,274 --> 00:10:09,109
YEAH. UH-HUH.

232
00:10:09,109 --> 00:10:11,111
I KNOW. I MISS YOU, TOO.

233
00:10:11,111 --> 00:10:12,446
I CAN'T WAIT TO SEE YOU.

234
00:10:12,446 --> 00:10:14,281
I LOVE YOU. BYE.

235
00:10:14,281 --> 00:10:16,450
OKAY, WHAT IS IN HERE, ROCKS?

236
00:10:16,450 --> 00:10:19,994
OH, NO. THIS IS MY COLLECTION
OF, UH, FOSSIL SAMPLES.

237
00:10:19,994 --> 00:10:21,955
SO ROCKS.

238
00:10:30,964 --> 00:10:33,467
I'M REALLY GOING
TO MISS THIS APARTMENT.

239
00:10:33,467 --> 00:10:35,802
YOU KNOW, BEN... BEN
TOOK HIS FIRST STEPS

240
00:10:35,802 --> 00:10:36,928
RIGHT OVER THERE.

241
00:10:36,928 --> 00:10:38,637
HMM.

242
00:10:38,637 --> 00:10:40,265
HEY, REMEMBER WHEN I
RAN INTO THIS THING

243
00:10:40,265 --> 00:10:42,434
AND IT KIND
OF KNOCKED ME OUT
A LITTLE, HUH?

244
00:10:44,102 --> 00:10:46,104
I LOVE THIS PLACE.

245
00:10:46,104 --> 00:10:48,898
TELL YOU THE TRUTH,
I WISH I DIDN'T HAVE TO MOVE.

246
00:10:48,898 --> 00:10:51,234
UH, ARE YOU SAYING
THAT YOU'RE

247
00:10:51,234 --> 00:10:54,195
NOT ENTIRELY HAPPY
ABOUT THIS?

248
00:10:54,195 --> 00:10:56,030
WELL, I MEAN,
IF, UH...

249
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:57,240
IF EMILY GAVE
ME A CHOICE...

250
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:59,534
YOU DO HAVE A CHOICE.

251
00:10:59,534 --> 00:11:01,869
ROSS, WHY ARE YOU
LISTENING TO HER?

252
00:11:01,869 --> 00:11:04,623
ARE YOU CRAZY?
WHAT?

253
00:11:04,623 --> 00:11:07,167
WELL, IT'S NOT RIGHT,
WHAT EMILY WANTS YOU TO DO.

254
00:11:07,167 --> 00:11:08,502
SHE IS TOTALLY... OW!

255
00:11:08,502 --> 00:11:10,504
STOP PINCHING ME.

256
00:11:10,504 --> 00:11:13,465
LOOK, NOW, YOU GUYS SAID
I ONLY HAVE TO
KEEP MY MOUTH SHUT

257
00:11:13,465 --> 00:11:15,716
AS LONG AS ROSS
WAS HAPPY, RIGHT?

258
00:11:15,716 --> 00:11:17,511
WELL, HE
JUST TOLD ME

259
00:11:17,511 --> 00:11:19,887
THAT HE'S NOT
ENTIRELY HAPPY.

260
00:11:22,015 --> 00:11:23,682
WHAT'S GOING ON?

261
00:11:23,682 --> 00:11:25,059
WE ALL HATE EMILY.

262
00:11:27,521 --> 00:11:28,605
NO.

263
00:11:28,605 --> 00:11:30,982
NO. ROSS,
WE DO NOT HATE EMILY.

264
00:11:30,982 --> 00:11:32,942
WE JUST...
WE JUST THINK

265
00:11:32,942 --> 00:11:36,279
THAT YOU'RE HAVING TO SACRIFICE
A WHOLE LOT TO MAKE HER HAPPY.

266
00:11:36,279 --> 00:11:38,281
YEAH.

267
00:11:38,281 --> 00:11:39,866
WE JUST THINK
THAT MAYBE SHE'S BEING

268
00:11:39,866 --> 00:11:42,577
A LITTLE... UNREASONABLE.

269
00:11:42,577 --> 00:11:44,703
YES. YES.
UNREASONABLE.

270
00:11:44,703 --> 00:11:47,123
UNREASONABLE?

271
00:11:47,123 --> 00:11:48,749
HOW ABOUT WE HAVE
THIS CONVERSATION

272
00:11:48,749 --> 00:11:50,793
WHEN ONE OF YOU GUYS
GETS MARRIED?

273
00:11:50,793 --> 00:11:52,253
YOU HAVE NO IDEA

274
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:54,755
WHAT IT TAKES
TO MAKE A MARRIAGE WORK.

275
00:11:54,755 --> 00:11:56,383
IT'S ABOUT COMPROMISE.

276
00:11:56,383 --> 00:11:59,010
DO YOU ALWAYS LIKE IT? NO.
DO YOU DO IT? YES.

277
00:11:59,010 --> 00:12:02,763
BECAUSE IT'S NOT ALL LAUGHING,
HAPPY, CANDY-IN-THE-SKY

278
00:12:02,763 --> 00:12:04,432
DRINKING-COFFEE-AT-CENTRAL-PERK
ALL THE TIME.

279
00:12:04,432 --> 00:12:06,142
IT'S REAL
LIFE, OKAY?

280
00:12:06,142 --> 00:12:09,020
IT'S WHAT GROWNUPS DO.

281
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:17,945
I THINK HE'S RIGHT.

282
00:12:17,945 --> 00:12:20,156
YOU GUYS HANG OUT
AT THE COFFEEHOUSE WAY TOO MUCH.

283
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:29,374
GOD, I FEEL SO GUILTY
ABOUT ROSS.

284
00:12:29,374 --> 00:12:30,749
I KNOW.

285
00:12:30,749 --> 00:12:33,545
I KIND OF FEEL
LIKE IT'S MY FAULT.

286
00:12:35,922 --> 00:12:37,924
KIND OF?

287
00:12:37,924 --> 00:12:40,635
IF YOU HAD JUST KEPT THIS
TO YOURSELF, NONE OF THIS
WOULD HAVE HAPPENED.

288
00:12:40,635 --> 00:12:43,471
WELL, I'M KEEPING SO MANY THINGS
TO MYSELF THESE DAYS

289
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:45,056
SOMETHING WAS BOUND TO SLIP OUT.

290
00:12:47,141 --> 00:12:49,018
WELL, I THINK
IT'S VERY BRAVE
WHAT YOU SAID.

291
00:12:49,018 --> 00:12:50,604
OH, YEAH.

292
00:12:50,604 --> 00:12:53,231
ALL RIGHT. I CAN'T
SIT HERE ANYMORE.

293
00:12:53,231 --> 00:12:55,858
I HAVE TO WALK PLACES.

294
00:12:55,858 --> 00:12:57,611
PHEEBS, WHAT ARE YOU DOING
WITH THE COAT?

295
00:12:57,611 --> 00:12:59,778
HOW ABOUT THE WHOLE
ANIMAL RIGHTS THING?

296
00:12:59,778 --> 00:13:03,199
WELL, I'VE BEEN READING UP,
AND FOR YOUR INFORMATION

297
00:13:03,199 --> 00:13:05,076
MINKS ARE NOT VERY NICE.

298
00:13:06,745 --> 00:13:09,872
OKAY, I ADMIT IT,
I LOVE THIS COAT, OKAY.

299
00:13:09,872 --> 00:13:12,709
IT'S THE BEST THING
I'VE EVER HAD WRAPPED AROUND ME

300
00:13:12,709 --> 00:13:15,462
INCLUDING PHIL HUNTLEY.

301
00:13:15,462 --> 00:13:18,298
REMEMBER PHIL HUNTLEY?
HE WAS FINE.

302
00:13:29,058 --> 00:13:30,059
HI.

303
00:13:33,438 --> 00:13:35,106
SO, YOU LIKE
THE SHORT HAIR BETTER?

304
00:13:35,106 --> 00:13:36,065
WHAT?

305
00:13:39,193 --> 00:13:40,903
YETI... DANNY?!

306
00:13:42,905 --> 00:13:46,867
HAD TO CUT MY HAIR TO GET RID
OF THE, UH... FOGGER SMELL.

307
00:13:46,867 --> 00:13:47,910
OH.

308
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:50,204
LISTEN, OH, I'M SO SORRY.

309
00:13:50,204 --> 00:13:52,206
I WOULD-I WOULD
HAVE NEVER FOGGED YOU

310
00:13:52,206 --> 00:13:55,710
YOU KNOW, IF YOU HADN'T
LOOKED SO, YOU KNOW, UH...

311
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:57,712
ABSOLUTELY.

312
00:13:57,712 --> 00:13:59,714
SOME PEOPLE ARE JUST
INTO APPEARANCES.

313
00:13:59,714 --> 00:14:01,174
WHAT?

314
00:14:01,174 --> 00:14:02,759
THAT'S COOL.
THAT'S COOL.

315
00:14:02,759 --> 00:14:03,760
WHOA! WHOA! NO!

316
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:05,178
NO, THAT IS NOT COOL.

317
00:14:05,178 --> 00:14:06,887
YOU-YOU DON'T
EVEN KNOW ME.

318
00:14:06,887 --> 00:14:08,765
COME ON. YOU'VE GOT
THE SHOPPING BAGS

319
00:14:08,765 --> 00:14:10,099
AND THE SAKS CATALOGUE.

320
00:14:10,099 --> 00:14:11,850
SO, UH, FROM THAT,
YOU THINK

321
00:14:11,850 --> 00:14:14,354
YOU'VE GOT ME
ALL FIGURED OUT?!

322
00:14:14,354 --> 00:14:16,063
WELL, YOU DON'T.

323
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:20,819
YOU KNOW, I COULD HAVE TOYS FOR
UNDERPRIVILEGED KIDS IN HERE.

324
00:14:20,819 --> 00:14:22,654
DO YOU?

325
00:14:22,654 --> 00:14:26,491
WELL, YOU KNOW, IF KIDS
LIKE TO PLAY WITH CAPRI PANTS.

326
00:14:26,491 --> 00:14:28,951
OKAY.

327
00:14:28,951 --> 00:14:31,037
AND STOP SAYING THAT.

328
00:14:31,037 --> 00:14:32,246
I HATE THAT.

329
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:33,414
OKAY.

330
00:14:44,509 --> 00:14:46,010
FINE.
I JUDGED YOU.

331
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:48,388
I MADE A SNAP JUDGMENT,
BUT YOU DID IT, TOO

332
00:14:48,388 --> 00:14:52,225
AND YOU'RE WORSE, BECAUSE
YOU ARE STICKING TO YOUR
STUPID SNAP JUDGMENT.

333
00:14:52,225 --> 00:14:54,394
YOU CAN'T EVEN
OPEN UP YOUR MIND
FOR A SECOND

334
00:14:54,394 --> 00:14:55,895
TO SEE THAT YOU
MIGHT BE WRONG.

335
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:57,271
WHAT DOES THAT
SAY ABOUT YOU?

336
00:14:57,271 --> 00:14:59,982
THAT PIZZA PLACE
ACROSS THE STREET ANY GOOD?

337
00:14:59,982 --> 00:15:01,942
WHAT?

338
00:15:01,942 --> 00:15:04,153
I'M HUNGRY.
WANT TO GET SOME PIZZA?

339
00:15:04,153 --> 00:15:05,697
YOU CAN KEEP YELLING
IF THERE'S MORE.

340
00:15:06,781 --> 00:15:08,157
OKAY.

341
00:15:08,157 --> 00:15:09,576
OKAY.

342
00:15:09,576 --> 00:15:10,702
STOP SAYING THAT.

343
00:15:10,702 --> 00:15:11,870
I HATE THAT.

344
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:18,585
UH, ROSS...

345
00:15:18,585 --> 00:15:20,420
ARE YOU STILL
MAD AT US?
YUP.

346
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:23,130
OH, GOOD, 'CAUSE WE HAVE
AN "I'M SORRY" SONG.

347
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:25,466
YOU KNOW WHAT?
I'M REALLY NOT IN THE MOOD.

348
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:29,596
LOOK, ROSS,
I FEEL REALLY BAD.

349
00:15:29,596 --> 00:15:32,557
I MEAN, YOU'RE GOING
THROUGH ALL THIS STUFF

350
00:15:32,557 --> 00:15:35,268
AND... I JUST ACTED
LIKE A JERK.

351
00:15:35,268 --> 00:15:37,144
YEAH, WE ARE SO SORRY.

352
00:15:37,144 --> 00:15:39,856
YOU'RE KIND OF
STEPPING ON THE SONG.

353
00:15:39,856 --> 00:15:42,609
LOOK... WE WERE WAY
OUT OF LINE, ALL RIGHT?

354
00:15:42,609 --> 00:15:44,360
WE TOTALLY SUPPORT YOU.

355
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,613
WHATEVER YOU DECIDE,
WHATEVER YOU DO.

356
00:15:46,613 --> 00:15:49,949
OKAY, NOW YOU'RE JUST TAKING
LINES RIGHT OUT OF THE SONG.

357
00:15:49,949 --> 00:15:52,702
LOOK, THIS IS HARD ENOUGH, OKAY.

358
00:15:52,702 --> 00:15:54,995
I REALLY NEED YOU GUYS
RIGHT NOW.

359
00:15:54,995 --> 00:15:56,163
YES. EXACTLY.

360
00:15:56,163 --> 00:15:58,082
AND THAT'S WHY...

361
00:15:58,082 --> 00:16:00,000
( strums two notes )

362
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,502
WHY DON'T YOU
COME OVER TONIGHT

363
00:16:01,502 --> 00:16:03,296
AND I'LL MAKE YOU
YOUR FAVORITE DINNER?

364
00:16:03,296 --> 00:16:05,799
COME ON.

365
00:16:05,799 --> 00:16:07,842
OKAY.

366
00:16:07,842 --> 00:16:09,552
THANKS, YOU GUYS.

367
00:16:09,552 --> 00:16:11,512
PHEEBS, ARE YOU
WEARING FUR?

368
00:16:11,512 --> 00:16:13,514
OKAY, LET'S GET SOME
PERSPECTIVE, PEOPLE.

369
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:16,601
IT'S NOT LIKE I'M WEARING
A SEEING-EYE DOG COAT.

370
00:16:19,729 --> 00:16:21,272
HEY, YOU KNOW, ROSS

371
00:16:21,272 --> 00:16:23,357
I, UH... I THINK
I KIND OF UNDERSTAND

372
00:16:23,357 --> 00:16:25,777
WHY I KIND OF LOST IT TODAY.

373
00:16:25,777 --> 00:16:27,612
YOU DO, HUH?

374
00:16:27,612 --> 00:16:31,157
YEAH, YOU SEE,
I'M AN ACTOR, RIGHT?

375
00:16:31,157 --> 00:16:35,578
SO I GOT TO KEEP MY EMOTIONS
RIGHT AT THE SURFACE, YOU KNOW?

376
00:16:35,578 --> 00:16:40,249
I GOT A LOT OF BALLS IN THE AIR,
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN?

377
00:16:40,249 --> 00:16:43,711
IT'S TOUGH. GUYS LIKE ME,
YOU KNOW, YOU WANDER AROUND--

378
00:16:43,711 --> 00:16:45,880
YOU'RE ALONE.

379
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:48,842
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

380
00:16:49,968 --> 00:16:52,428
I'M NOT SURE.

381
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:53,972
HI.

382
00:16:53,972 --> 00:16:55,932
HEY, LOOK AT YOU.
WHERE HAVE YOU BEEN?

383
00:16:55,932 --> 00:17:00,144
OH, I WENT TO HAVE
PIZZA WITH DANNY.

384
00:17:00,144 --> 00:17:04,398
HOW DID THAT HAPPEN?
THAT YETI IS ONE SMOOTH TALKER.

385
00:17:04,398 --> 00:17:06,860
I HOPE YOU'RE NOT TOO FULL,
'CAUSE DINNER'S ALMOST READY.

386
00:17:06,860 --> 00:17:08,653
YEAH, YOU KNOW, I THINK

387
00:17:08,653 --> 00:17:10,321
I'M PROBABLY JUST GOING
TO HANG OUT IN ROOM.

388
00:17:10,321 --> 00:17:12,198
OH, NO.
WHY?

389
00:17:12,198 --> 00:17:13,658
COME ON,
YOU GUYS.

390
00:17:13,658 --> 00:17:16,118
IF EMILY KNEW I WAS HERE
HAVING DINNER WITH YOU

391
00:17:16,118 --> 00:17:17,912
SHE WOULD FLIP OUT
AND YOU KNOW IT.

392
00:17:19,956 --> 00:17:23,001
IT'S OKAY.
I REALLY... I DON'T MIND.

393
00:17:23,001 --> 00:17:24,168
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT.

394
00:17:24,168 --> 00:17:26,337
YOU KNOW WHAT? JUST STAY.

395
00:17:26,337 --> 00:17:30,717
PLEASE. IT WOULD REALLY MEAN
A LOT FOR ME IF YOU STAY.

396
00:17:32,092 --> 00:17:33,469
ROSS, I JUST...

397
00:17:33,469 --> 00:17:37,181
RACHEL, PLEASE.
JUST HAVE DINNER WITH US.

398
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:40,309
OKAY, OKAY, JOEY, IT'S OKAY.
SETTLE DOWN.

399
00:17:40,309 --> 00:17:41,811
ALL RIGHT. I'M SORRY.

400
00:17:41,811 --> 00:17:43,062
I'M SORRY.

401
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:45,189
YOU SEE, RACH, I'M AN ACTOR.

402
00:17:48,317 --> 00:17:49,777
HEY!

403
00:17:49,777 --> 00:17:52,864
HEY, LOOK,
THE UGLY NAKED GUY'S BACK.

404
00:17:52,864 --> 00:17:54,991
OH, MY GOD!

405
00:17:54,991 --> 00:17:57,159
WE HAVEN'T SEEN HIM
IN SO LONG.

406
00:17:57,159 --> 00:18:00,120
OH, GOD, I REALLY MISSED
THAT FAT BASTARD.

407
00:18:03,750 --> 00:18:06,002
WOW. THIS IS
SO WEIRD.

408
00:18:06,002 --> 00:18:07,795
I JUST REALIZED THIS
MAY BE THE LAST TIME

409
00:18:07,795 --> 00:18:09,255
WE'RE ALL HANGING
OUT TOGETHER.

410
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:13,760
IT'S ALMOST
AS IF HE KNEW.

411
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:15,428
( phone ringing )

412
00:18:15,428 --> 00:18:17,346
I'LL GET IT.

413
00:18:20,266 --> 00:18:21,434
HELLO.

414
00:18:21,434 --> 00:18:22,810
HI, EMILY.

415
00:18:24,854 --> 00:18:27,648
YEAH, YOU TRACKED HIM DOWN.
HOLD ON ONE SECOND.

416
00:18:29,901 --> 00:18:31,485
HEY.

417
00:18:31,485 --> 00:18:33,613
YEAH, YEAH,
WE'RE, UH...

418
00:18:33,613 --> 00:18:35,865
WE'RE JUST
HAVING DINNER.

419
00:18:35,865 --> 00:18:37,366
UH, YEAH, SURE. HOLD ON.

420
00:18:37,366 --> 00:18:38,618
SHE WANTS TO SAY HI.

421
00:18:38,618 --> 00:18:39,577
HOLD ON.

422
00:18:42,747 --> 00:18:44,123
All:
HI, EMILY.

423
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:45,541
HELLO, EVERYONE.

424
00:18:45,541 --> 00:18:48,044
SO, WHO AM I SAYING HELLO TO?

425
00:18:48,044 --> 00:18:49,712
WELL, UH...

426
00:18:49,712 --> 00:18:51,213
I DON'T KNOW ABOUT
WHO'S HERE

427
00:18:51,213 --> 00:18:52,715
BUT I CAN TELL YOU
FOR DAMN SURE

428
00:18:52,715 --> 00:18:54,926
WHO'S NOT HERE,
AND THAT'S RACHEL.

429
00:18:56,886 --> 00:18:58,512
Well, I should hope not.

430
00:18:58,512 --> 00:19:01,682
Ross knows better
than that by now.

431
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:06,145
YOU KNOW WHAT?

432
00:19:06,145 --> 00:19:07,271
RACHEL IS HERE.

433
00:19:07,271 --> 00:19:09,148
She's there?

434
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:10,900
OH, YEAH, THERE SHE IS.

435
00:19:12,110 --> 00:19:15,071
YEAH, YEAH, SHE'S HERE.

436
00:19:15,071 --> 00:19:17,115
ROSS, TAKE ME OFF SPEAKER PHONE.

437
00:19:17,115 --> 00:19:18,950
HI.

438
00:19:18,950 --> 00:19:21,661
HOW COULD YOU DO THIS TO ME?

439
00:19:21,661 --> 00:19:24,747
I THOUGHT I'D MADE MY FEELINGS
ABOUT RACHEL PERFECTLY CLEAR.

440
00:19:24,747 --> 00:19:28,960
LOOK, EMILY, I'M JUST HAVING
DINNER WITH MY FRIENDS, OKAY?

441
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:31,129
YOU OBVIOUSLY CAN'T
KEEP AWAY FROM HER.

442
00:19:31,129 --> 00:19:32,505
Emily, that's ridiculous.

443
00:19:32,505 --> 00:19:34,507
LOOK, I'M MOVING FOR YOU.

444
00:19:34,507 --> 00:19:37,135
I'M CUTTING FRIENDS
OUT OF MY LIFE FOR YOU.

445
00:19:37,135 --> 00:19:41,514
PLEASE, JUST GET ON THE PLANE
AND COME TO NEW YORK, OKAY?
YOU'LL SEE.

446
00:19:41,514 --> 00:19:44,017
You're the only person
I want to be with.

447
00:19:44,017 --> 00:19:45,977
I'LL FEEL BETTER WHEN I'M THERE

448
00:19:45,977 --> 00:19:48,521
AND I CAN KNOW WHERE YOU ARE
ALL THE TIME.

449
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:51,524
WELL, YOU...

450
00:19:51,524 --> 00:19:54,777
YOU CAN'T KNOW WHERE I AM
ALL THE TIME.

451
00:19:56,278 --> 00:19:58,364
LOOK, THIS MARRIAGE IS
NEVER GOING TO WORK

452
00:19:58,364 --> 00:20:00,033
IF YOU DON'T TRUST ME.

453
00:20:01,784 --> 00:20:03,161
YOU'RE RIGHT.

454
00:20:04,537 --> 00:20:08,166
SO... CAN YOU TRUST ME?

455
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:14,505
NO.

456
00:20:17,424 --> 00:20:19,760
I THINK IT'S
GOING OKAY.

457
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:21,762
YEAH, LOOKS LIKE
HE'S SMILING.

458
00:20:21,762 --> 00:20:23,181
HOW CAN YOU TELL?

459
00:20:23,181 --> 00:20:24,849
YOU CAN ONLY SEE
THE BACK OF HIS HEAD.

460
00:20:24,849 --> 00:20:26,976
YOU CAN TOTALLY TELL.

461
00:20:26,976 --> 00:20:29,020
HERE, LOOK, WATCH ME.

462
00:20:30,270 --> 00:20:33,066
SMILE. FROWN.
SMILE.

463
00:20:33,066 --> 00:20:35,651
FROWN... SMILE...

464
00:20:49,289 --> 00:20:51,291
WELL, I GUESS THAT'S IT.

465
00:20:51,291 --> 00:20:52,292
Phoebe:
WHAT?

466
00:20:52,292 --> 00:20:54,170
WHAT HAPPENED?
WHAT HAPPENED?

467
00:20:54,170 --> 00:20:55,963
MY MARRIAGE IS OVER.

468
00:20:55,963 --> 00:20:57,464
Monica:
SWEETIE...

469
00:20:57,464 --> 00:20:59,842
OH, LOOK AT YOU.

470
00:20:59,842 --> 00:21:02,386
YOU'RE SHIVERING.

471
00:21:02,386 --> 00:21:03,554
HERE.

472
00:21:07,349 --> 00:21:10,686
ROSS, HONEY, IS THERE
ANYTHING WE CAN DO?

473
00:21:12,396 --> 00:21:13,564
YEAH.

474
00:21:15,191 --> 00:21:18,111
YOU CAN HELP ME GET
MY FURNITURE BACK FROM GUNTHER.

475
00:21:26,786 --> 00:21:29,705
( whistling tune )

